lcos-updates (0.9.4-6) unstable; urgency=high

  * Security: stop running installs with DEBCONF_DEBUG=developer. Its
    protocol trace (SET and reply lines) carried answer values, including
    preseeded and script-set passwords, and apt copied it into
    /var/log/apt/term.log before the helper could strip it.
  * Questions a normal install would ask are now found by running debconf
    with DEBCONF_NONINTERACTIVE_SEEN=true and listing questions that turned
    seen during the install; debconf applies the priority itself.
  * Regression tests check that no secret reaches term.log, helper output,
    or the install environment.

 -- Phil <phil@brushpad.local>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0500

lcos-updates (0.9.4-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix round 13 review findings for debconf reporting:
    - Password questions (passwords.dat) are reported as "left blank" or
      "set, not shown"; the value never leaves the helper.
    - Only answers that are new or changed by this install are listed, so
      a later upgrade does not repeat them.
    - Only questions a normal install would ask at the configured debconf
      priority (default high) are listed, by their question text. The
      install runs with DEBCONF_DEBUG=developer to see the priorities; that
      trace is stripped from all output.
    - A partly failed install still lists the answers it chose.
    - The review notice says earlier answers are kept and new questions get
      the suggested answer, and points to the Terminal app.
    - Check inspects new packages' debs for a templates member, so a new
      package that uses debconf without depending on it is flagged.

