lcos-updates (0.9-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Closing after an install that already finished reports that result and
    does not leave Check stuck. The same outcome text is used for the
    window and the notification.
  * A finished install keeps phased, held, and kept-back packages from the
    check, and says "You're up to date" only when nothing is left.
  * Once dpkg has started, the install is not killed for idle time or the
    hard cap. A stall shows how long the phase has run, and after a long
    stall the shutdown inhibitor is relaxed.
  * Package-list errors keep apt's own lines. A proxy or offline hint is
    added only when that cause is plausible.
  * A full disk shows dpkg's cause. dpkg --configure -a is mentioned only
    after an interrupted dpkg has exited.
  * A restart sentence is printed once, after "Updates installed." A
    reboot-required flag that was already there is not called this install.
  * A package kept back because another package would be removed is
    described as a removal.
  * Apt's carriage-return download progress is shown in the window.

